Sanctorum opening, unnumbered, no. 1810, column R, marked P; artifact PDF p. 509","verification_source_id":"passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.phase2-comm-s-saturnini-martyris-orations-recheck-2026-10-22"},"publication":{"basis":"public-domain","evidence":"Whole petition and short conclusion preexist on 1862 p.364, not in the later standalone referral. The 1862 printing is public domain in the United States. Under 17 U.S.C. 103(b), the 1962 edition contributes no new right in this preexisting complete petition. Explicit spelling, pointing and conclusion-length transformations follow guidance/propers-for-agents.md; the restricted control artifact is not publication authority.","locator":"Pustet 1862 printed p. 364, R, Pro S. Saturnino. Secreta in Vigilia S. Andreae; original PDF p. 450; retained extract p. 2","source_ids":["artifact.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-10-22.phase2-octnov-commemorations-20261022","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.phase2-octnov-commemoration-pages-20261022"],"status":"permitted","surfaces":["cli","corpus-data","download","print","public-git","web"]},"reason":null,"text_sha256":"4bb23534461afb16e55498de1841c0212b423e44c36c788b46f5781e4429a79b","withheld":false},"name":"Secret","source":"composed","taken_from":null,"text":"Munera, Domine, tibi dicata sanctifica: et, intercedente beato\nSaturnino Martyre tuo, per haec eadem nos placatus intende. Per\nDominum.\n","text_status":null,"translations":[{"caution":"A pre-1955 lay hand missal, not an approved liturgical translation and never an altar book. Its rubrics, its seasonal second and third orations, its Holy Week and its sanctoral are not those of 1962. It is carried only where a 1962 formulary is the same prayer, and nothing here may be used for recitation.\n\nThe 1861 keeps 29 November in its temporal, at the Vigil of St Andrew; leaf n530, printed p. 522, carries the commemoration's Collect, which this file already records, and leaf n531, printed p. 523, running head `29th NOVEMBER.`, carries `SECRET, of St. SATURNINUS.` with no Latin cue. It answers `Munera, Domine, tibi dicata sanctifica`. Page-image collation confirms that this historical English body answers the complete target Latin identity; publication is limited to the 1861 wording and does not claim that Cummiskey appoints the 1962 celebration.","lang":"en","rights":"public-domain","source_id":"edition.eugene-cummiskey.roman-missal-english-laity.philadelphia-1861","source_label":"The Roman Missal translated into the English language for the use of the laity, first revised edition (Philadelphia: Eugene Cummiskey, 1861)","text":"Sanctify, O Lord, the offerings we have consecrated to thee, and being appeased thereby, mercifully look down upon us, by the intercession of blessed Saturninus, thy Martyr. Thro'."}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"citations":[{"book":"John","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":12,"first":26,"last":26}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":12,"first":26,"last":26}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":12,"first":26,"last":26}]},"ref":"John 12:26","token":"John","unresolved":null}],"coverage":{"component":"scripture","cycle":"all","cycle_family":null,"languages":[{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"la","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]},{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"en","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]}],"occurrence_id":"roman-1962%3Acomm-s-saturnini-martyris%3Amain%3A10:all:all","schema":"triptych-missal-unit-coverage/v1","target_id":"roman-1962%3Aproper%3Acommune-unius-martyris-4%3Amain%3ACommunion%3A1:all:all"},"cycles":{},"form":"","form_id":"main","incipit":null,"languages":[{"available":false,"held":false,"lang":"la","reason":"delegated-to-scripture","status":"scripture-delegated"},{"available":false,