e-image collation and exact bounded editorial projection","provenance_confidence":"high","provenance_evidence":"Complete page-image comparison, not an incipit or former-body-hash reconstruction. The bounded project passage reproduces this exact Unicode hash. The separate historical passage passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.phase2-comm-s-saturnini-martyris-orations-page-image-2026-10-22 records the printed antecedent. Differences: Historical short Per Dominum. appears at the head of p.365. Target expanded conclusion ends in unitate. Pointing/capitals/accents/ligatures.","relationship":"editorial-projection-exact-to-target","source_date":"2026-10-22 project editorial projection; antecedent Pustet Ratisbon 1862","source_id":"passage.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-10-22.phase2-comm-s-saturnini-martyris-postcommunion","status":"collated","transformations":["join printed line wraps","remove stress accents","expand ae/oe ligatures","apply target punctuation and capitals","retain declared project consonantal j","carry the target conclusion at its actual printed length"],"verification_locator":"1962 printed p. Proprium Sanctorum opening, unnumbered, no. 1811, column R, marked P; artifact PDF p. 509","verification_source_id":"passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.phase2-comm-s-saturnini-martyris-orations-recheck-2026-10-22"},"publication":{"basis":"public-domain","evidence":"Whole petition preexists across 1862 pp.364-365; the final acceptos and printed conclusion were checked, not inferred from the incipit. The 1862 printing is public domain in the United States. Under 17 U.S.C. 103(b), the 1962 edition contributes no new right in this preexisting complete petition. Explicit spelling, pointing and conclusion-length transformations follow guidance/propers-for-agents.md; the restricted control artifact is not publication authority.","locator":"Pustet 1862 printed p. 364/365, R bottom to L top, Pro sancto Saturnino. Postcommunio in Vigilia S. Andreae; original PDF p. 450/451; retained extract p. 2/3","source_ids":["artifact.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-10-22.phase2-octnov-commemorations-20261022","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.phase2-octnov-commemoration-pages-20261022"],"status":"permitted","surfaces":["cli","corpus-data","download","print","public-git","web"]},"reason":null,"text_sha256":"ad9e7c1a738581515156c43f62c5bb98290117f10b98a3bb73431fa603a7e6ab","withheld":false},"name":"Postcommunion","source":"composed","taken_from":null,"text":"Sanctificet nos, quaesumus, Domine, tui perceptio sacramenti: et\nintercessione Sanctorum tuorum tibi reddat acceptos. Per Dominum\nnostrum Jesum Christum, Filium tuum: Qui tecum vivit et regnat in\nunitate.\n","text_status":null,"translations":[{"caution":"A pre-1955 lay hand missal, not an approved liturgical translation and never an altar book. Its rubrics, its seasonal second and third orations, its Holy Week and its sanctoral are not those of 1962. It is carried only where a 1962 formulary is the same prayer, and nothing here may be used for recitation.\n\nSame leaf as the Secret above, headed `P. COMM. Sanctificet, of St. SATURNINUS.`, answering `Sanctificet nos, quaesumus Domine`. The page prints no conclusion. Page-image collation confirms that this historical English body answers the complete target Latin identity; publication is limited to the 1861 wording and does not claim that Cummiskey appoints the 1962 celebration.","lang":"en","rights":"public-domain","source_id":"edition.eugene-cummiskey.roman-missal-english-laity.philadelphia-1861","source_label":"The Roman Missal translated into the English language for the use of the laity, first revised edition (Philadelphia: Eugene Cummiskey, 1861)","text":"May the receiving of this thy sacrament, O Lord, we beseech thee, sanctify us: and by the intercession of thy saints, make us acceptable to thee."}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"appointment_identity":{"form_id":"main","mass":"commune-unius-martyris-4","occurrence":1,"proper":"Epistle (altera in Communi unius Martyris)"},"citations":[{"book":"James","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":1,"first":2,"last":12}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":1,"first":2,"last":12}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":1,"first":2,"last":12}]},"ref":"James 1:2-12","token":"James","unresolved":null}],"coverage":{"component":"scripture","cycle":"all","cycle_family":null,"languages":[{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"la","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]},{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"en","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]}],"occurrence_id":"roman-1962%3Acomm-s-saturnini-martyris%3Amain%3A12:all:all","schema":"triptych-missal-unit-coverage/v1","target_id":"roman-1962%3Aproper%3Acommune-unius-martyris-1%3Amain%3AEpistle%2520%2528altera%2520in%2520Communi%2520unius%2520Martyris%2529%3A1:all:all"},"cycles":{},"form":"","form_id":"main","incipit":null,"languages":[{"available":false,"held":false,"lang":"la","reason":"delegated-to-scripture","status":"scripture-delegated"},{"available":false,"held":false,"lang":"en","reason":"delegated-to-scripture","status":"scripture-delegated"}],"latin":null,"name":"Epistle (altera in Communi unius Martyris)","ordinary_disposition":{"anchor":{"form_id":"main","mass":"commune-unius-martyris-4","occurrence":1,"proper":"Epistle"},"basis":"1962 Common opening artifact809/[1] paragraph1; 1962 CMAA facsimile, artifact p. 817, printed [9]; raw text page line 33; Printed text unit 4237; Same-Common permission809/[1] paragraph1 plus family-wide additional Epistle at817/[9]. Printed Common is extra tempus paschale.","group":"unius-martyris-4-first-reading","kind":"alternative","option":"unit-4237"},"source":"